# .dockerignore (ENC-790 / H6)
#
# The Docker build context is this repo root. Without this file, host build
# artifacts get copied into the image — most damagingly build*/CMakeCache.txt,
# which hard-codes absolute host paths and makes the in-image `cmake` fail.
# Keep the context to source + build inputs only; the image fetches its own
# deps via apt (boost/rapidjson/openssl) + FetchContent (googletest).

# CMake / build output (the actual H6 breakage)
build/
build*/
out/
cmake-build-*/
CMakeFiles/
CMakeCache.txt
cmake_install.cmake
CTestTestfile.cmake
install_manifest.txt
compile_commands.json
*.ninja
.ninja_deps
.ninja_log

# Compiled artifacts
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.lib
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll
*.exe
*.out

# VCS / CI / editor cruft
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.code-workspace

# Visual Studio / MSBuild project files
*.vcxproj
*.vcxproj.*
*.sln
ALL_BUILD.*
ZERO_CHECK.*

# Vendored deps — not needed; the image installs boost/rapidjson/openssl via apt
third_party/

# Docs / specs — not build inputs
docs/
specs/
*.md
LICENSE

# Local runtime / logs
.run/
*.log
*.tmp
